course: dictionary
lesson: 11897
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. The context is the words and sentences around the word. «She wiped her brow after running up the stairs.» People wipe sweat from their forehead, so brow means forehead here.
explain: «She raised her brows in surprise.» Brows is the plural of brow, and here it means eyebrows, the hairs above your eyes. The clue is raised, because that is what eyebrows do when you are surprised.
explain: «The car slowed down at the brow of the hill.» Now brow means the top of the hill, where the road starts to slope down. A forehead would make no sense on a hill, so ask: what word would fit here? The context points to the top.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right. If it sounds silly, try another meaning.
fact: A brow is your forehead, the part of your face above your eyes.
fact: A brow can also be an eyebrow, and brows is the plural word for eyebrows.
fact: The brow of a hill is its top, where the ground starts to slope down.
fact: «Furrowed brow» means wrinkles on the forehead, often from thinking hard or worrying.
fact: Drivers must not overtake on the brow of a hill, because they cannot see what is coming over the top.
exercise: «He wiped his brow with his sleeve.» What does brow mean here? | *Forehead | Cheek | Eyebrow hair | Top of a hill
exercise: «The path went over the brow of the hill, and the sea came into view.» What does brow mean here? | Bottom of the valley | Forehead | Eyebrow | *Top of the hill
exercise: «Her brows went up when she heard the news.» What are her brows? | Her cheeks | Her hair ribbons | *Her eyebrows | Her shoes
test: «He had a furrowed brow all day because he was worried about the test.» What does a furrowed brow show? | *Worry or hard thinking | Being asleep | Laughing a lot | Feeling cold and wet
test: Drivers must not overtake on the brow of a hill. Why not? | *They cannot see what is coming over the top | It is always raining there | The road is too wide there | The hill is made of sand
exam: Ali says brow always means eyebrow. Is he right? | No, brow means a kind of shoe | Yes, brow only ever means eyebrow | Yes, but only on a hill | *No, brow can mean a forehead, an eyebrow or the top of a hill
